# plaso-dl

Learning-purpose CLI to batch download Plaso historical live-class recordings via HLS.

Non-goals:
- No DRM/decryption support.
- No bypassing paywalls, CAPTCHAs, or platform protections.

## Setup

1) Install Python 3.10+
2) Create venv and install:

```bash
cd D:\Project\plaso-dl
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\python -m pip install -U pip
.venv\Scripts\python -m pip install -e .[dev]
```

3) Ensure `ffmpeg` is available in PATH:

```bash
ffmpeg -version
```

## Usage

Set your token (captured from the desktop app DevTools request header `access-token`):

```bash
python -m plaso_dl auth set-token "<your-token>"
```

Or auto-capture token (recommended):

```bash
python -m plaso_dl auth auto-capture --host 127.0.0.1 --port 9222 --timeout 180
```

Before running auto-capture, start Plaso with remote debugging enabled:

```bash
"D:\PlasoCloud\plaso-yxt.exe" --remote-debugging-port=9222
```

List courses:

```bash
python -m plaso_dl courses list
```

Download a few:

```bash
python -m plaso_dl download all --out "D:/Project/plaso-dl/downloads" --limit 3
```
